# System Discovery

The system-specific outcome that the complete active system H2 population must search for and account for. Apply `common.md` and `designs.md` in the same pass for broader production contracts.

## Work-specific system requirements {#work-specific-system-requirements}

Discover every production-specific coupled-process condition required by the actual lighting, environment, effect, simulation, sound, or service domains. State authority, dependency and update order, clocks and seeking, seeds, resource and accuracy budgets, convergence or stability, cross-owner interfaces, degradation, recovery, and fallback are possible search directions rather than a checklist. Derive the requirements from the governed process, consumed design interfaces, target runtime, delivery or library use, and promised observations rather than a generic simulation or service architecture, and give each material result an actual system H2 owner or a production-local principle, obligation, or evidence relationship with a typed claim.

A positive acknowledgement identifies the current authored owners and contract wiring. If the complete search finds no independent system result, one population-wide exclusion names the concrete authority, dependency, clock, budget, stability, interface, degradation, recovery, and observation risks examined and the shared owners that fully cover them. A solver name, effect label, frame rate, or quality preset without its governed state, resource boundary, failure behavior, and observable result does not cover this duty.

Review question: which coupled-process condition is specific to these domains, budgets, or failure modes and absent from the reusable system contract?

Sources: [NASA systems engineering handbook on design boundaries, interfaces, timing, capacities, and technical performance measures](https://www.nasa.gov/reference/systems-engineering-handbook/); [NASA software verification guidance on operational constraints, interfaces, worst cases, recovery, and resource measurements](https://swehb.nasa.gov/spaces/SWEHBVB/pages/32604539/SWE-067%2B-%2BVerify%2BImplementation)
